    "diagnosis": "<p>Polyostotic fibrous dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Polyostotic fibrous dysplasia with localizations in proximal femur, pubic bone extending through inferior ramus to acetabulum, and left iliac bone. The lesions have sclerotic, well-defined, lobulated margins and a geographical pattern of destruction, and they exhibit a combination of osteolysis, ground-glass opacities, and sclerotic septations. Also note the varus deformation (shepherd&rsquo;s crook) of the right femur, which eventually resulted in a fracture. </p>",
    "source": "<p>Hans Bloem</p>",
